  "sport": "hockey",
  "title": "Half moon – goalie warm-up",
  "description": "The players stand in a half circle in front of one net, each with a puck. They shoot in turn from one end of the arc to the other, so the goalie has to move and face shots from different angles.\n\nStart with wrist shots and build up. Change direction, shoot from alternate sides, or call a number for who shoots next. Mix shots along the ice with shots to the glove and blocker. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Wait until the goalie is set and has seen the puck before you shoot."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Easy shots first – the goalie should get warm, not hurt."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Goalie: follow the puck and shuffle sideways between shots."
    }
  ],
